<!--
  M15 — the home screen sized for the HAND. PHONE values; the TV keeps its own set verbatim in
  `values-television/dimens_home.xml`, so the 10-foot design does not move.

  Measured on a 914x411dp landscape handset before anything was changed:

  - The hero BAND is a fixed 360dp. That is 67% of a 540dp television and **88% of this phone**,
    which is why Continue Watching was a sliver at the bottom edge with the gesture pill over it.
    This is the density complaint in one number.
  - Every action on the screen was under the 48dp touch minimum: Play Now 125x31.6dp, More Info
    112x30dp, the favourite button 30x30dp, and each nav rail item 34x34dp.

  One honest shortfall, stated rather than glossed: the rail cannot give all of its items 48dp.
  Six destinations plus Settings plus the profile mark in a 411dp column need ~431dp at 48dp each.
  They get 40dp instead, across the rail's full 60dp width — a 60x40dp target, still larger in area
  than the 48x48dp minimum but 8dp short in one dimension. 40dp is what the arithmetic allows once
  the header, divider, Settings row and profile mark are subtracted; 44dp overflowed by 30dp. The
  alternative was making a six-item nav rail scroll, which is worse. Raised for the owner rather
  than hidden.

  The rail's spacing is then arithmetic, not taste. Measured, the list gets 236dp between the logo
  and the divider; six items at 40dp + a 3dp gap need 258dp, and the sixth destination was sliced in
  half. Item gap 0 (a rail's items are meant to be contiguous — the highlight capsule separates
  them), a 4dp list inset and a 34dp profile mark bring the requirement to 240dp inside 243dp.
  NOTE: that fits SIX destinations. A seventh will scroll rather than clip, because rv_sidebar is
  now bottom-constrained, but it should be re-measured.

  The hero band keeps the design's 20dp overhang over the text section (268 vs 248, as 360 vs 340
  on the TV). 248dp is sized for the WORST case, not the average one: a featured title that wraps
  to two lines. At 22sp that case needed a 262dp section and pushed Continue Watching 9dp off the
  bottom, so the title is 18sp here — which the 1.6x scale still renders at ~29sp.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <dimen name="home_hero_band_height">268dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_section_height">248dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_title_size">18sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_desc_size">8sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_btn_height">48dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_btn_margin">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_hero_fav_size">48dp</dimen>

    <!-- Navigation rail -->
    <dimen name="home_nav_item_height">40dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_item_margin">0dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_item_width">60dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_item_inset">0dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_header_size">28dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_list_margin_top">4dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="home_nav_profile_size">34dp</dimen>
</resources>
